  "body": "`add_operation` answers: \"a Wire Contour names no EDM condition - choose one of machine Sodick ALC400G's conditions (it states none - add edm.conditions to the machine file)\". A user must write their own .mch before anything works. Related: #3183 (conditions from the machine's own table), #2130 (guide heights), #1500.\n\nDone means: the built-in Sodick machine ships with a documented starter condition set (marked as examples to replace), threader and guide-height fields, so a first Wire Contour generates and posts; the guide says how to replace them with the machine's own.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
